From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:50:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Implement IPersistMoniker, IProvideClassInfo,
 IOleCommandTarget and IServiceProvider for documents.

Documents of every version offer them on Windows; tools/msxmlmoreprobe
in the wine-altars repository asked each class what they answer:

- IProvideClassInfo gives the coclass of the version, DOMDocument or
  DOMDocument60, free-threaded or not;
- IOleCommandTarget supports no command, knows no command group, and
  takes OLECMDID_STOP;
- IServiceProvider has no services without a site, MSXML 6.0 clearing
  the output then and 3.0 leaving it alone; with a site it asks the
  site;
- IPersistMoniker keeps the moniker it is given even when it cannot
  load from it, answers E_INVALIDARG without a bind context and E_FAIL
  when the moniker cannot be bound to a stream, and hands the moniker
  back from GetCurMoniker without a reference of its own.

GetClassID names the class a document was created as: the
version-independent DOMDocument for MSXML 3.0, the free-threaded
classes for free-threaded documents.

MSXML 6.0's documents and the free-threaded ones also offer the
free-threaded marshaler on Windows.  Not here: this DOM takes no locks,
and other apartments would call it at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

